' PLAYDEMO.mml - a little march written as QB64-PE PLAY strings (MML).
'
' MID2SND and PCSEDIT read this the way QB64-PE's PLAY does. The PLAY line
' below is ordinary QB64-PE code (try it in a program): each string after a
' comma is another voice. In a string, a comma after a note plays the next
' note with it, so "E2,G2" is a two-note chord.
'
'   voice 1  the tune         O2 (in QB64-PE, O2 C is middle C)
'   voice 2  chords           O1, two notes each
'   voice 3  the bass         O0
'
PLAY "T132 MN O2 L8 G>CEGEC<G>C D4<B4G2 >C<B>CDEDC<B A4>D4C2", "T132 MN O1 L2 E,GE,G D,GD,F E,GD,G F,AE,G", "T132 MN O0 L4 CGCG GDG2 CGFC FGC2"
